// ============================================================
// Alloy structural sidecar: {{AREA}}
// Intent: specs/{{AREA}}.intent.json (kind: contract, v{{VERSION}})
// Last modified: {{DATE}}
//
// OPTIONAL — the structural backend. Only areas that declare
// formal_model.alloy_file use this file at all.
//
// Division of labour, deliberately strict:
//   Quint/Apalache  → BEHAVIOUR. Actions, traces, reachability,
//                     witnesses, conformance replay.
//   Alloy           → STRUCTURE. Cardinality, referential
//                     integrity, ownership, role lattices —
//                     relational facts that hold of every legal
//                     configuration, with no notion of time.
//
// Do NOT model state transitions here (Alloy 6 can, but two
// models of the same behaviour give two answers, and then the
// spec has no single source of truth). If the question mentions
// "after", "then", or "eventually", it belongs in the .qnt.
//
// Each INV-* routed here is a `///` record on its assertion
// (`/// @inv INV-NNN` + its statement + `@criticality`): hosting
// it on `assert <name>` implies proof: structural and
// alloy_command: <name>. spec-record runs `alloy exec -c <name>`
// and records the verdict; spec-lint FAILs if no check names it.
// ============================================================

module {{MODULE_NAME}}

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// SIGNATURES
// One sig per entity in concepts.entities[]. Keep the names
// identical to the intent file — reviewers read them side by side.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// {{SIGNATURES}}
// Example:
//   sig User {}
//   sig Account { owner: one User }
//
// `one`/`lone`/`some`/`set` on a field IS the cardinality
// constraint — most referential-integrity bugs die here.

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// FACTS
// Assumptions about every legal structure. A fact silently
// removes counterexamples, so anything that is really an
// environment assumption belongs in the intent file too, where a
// reviewer can see it.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// {{FACTS}}

// ------------------------------------------------------------
// ASSERTIONS + CHECKS — one pair per structural INV-*
//
// ALWAYS declare the scope explicitly. With no `for` clause
// Alloy silently uses 3, and a bound nobody wrote down is a
// bound nobody reviewed — spec-lint WARNs, and FAILs at review.
//
// The optional `expect 0` makes the CLI exit non-zero when a
// counterexample turns up, so the check also works as a plain
// CI assertion without any spec tooling installed.
// ------------------------------------------------------------

// {{ASSERTIONS}}
// Example:
//   assert noOrphanAccounts {
//     all a: Account | a.owner in User
//   }
//   check noOrphanAccounts for 3 Account, 3 User expect 0
//
// A ✓ here means: no counterexample EXISTS AT THIS SIZE. It is
// not a proof. Widening the scope strengthens the claim; the
// readback always prints the scope next to the ✓ so the claim
// and its bound travel together.
